-{"externalId": "amy", "kind": "partner", "level": 1, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 20, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Amy", "role": "The vale's quiet connector — Amberford. Looks after rather a lot of things, none of them hers; Hearthholt's affairs (taxes, gutters, chimneys swept for no one) one thread among hundreds, kept well because she keeps everything well.", "focus": 22, "hpMax": 20, "level": 1, "notes": "First sister — UNMET, intro order 1. Intro hook: the keys leave her locked drawer at dusk the moment he crosses; she climbs the hill the same evening with supper packed before she knows whom she'll meet (Kept's first-ever firing — her hands sure of a stranger; she will not know what it means). Voice her ONLY via the fresh amy seat from her first line onward (gmContext policy amy-seat-voice). GM-EYES: Kept fate-basis is deep fog.", "stats": {"Mind": 15, "Grace": 11, "Might": 8, "Essence": 12, "Presence": 14, "Vitality": 10}, "aspect": "Hearth", "skills": [{"name": "Stewardship", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Reading People", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Provisioning", "rank": 3}, {"name": "Letters & Accounts", "rank": 2}], "talent": {"name": "Kept", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "Fate-based: fires for anyone she is GOING to have sex with in the future, before either knows — see the gmReference roster entry \"amy\" (Talent line). It has NEVER YET FIRED; she does not know she carries it in these terms."}, "stamMax": 20, "stamina": 20, "focusMax": 22, "bondStage": "Stranger", "appearance": {"face": "Blonde, fair-skinned — coloring that takes lamplight and morning light kindly. Blue eyes that do most of her listening: steady, warm, attentive; you feel read before you feel looked at. Handsome rather than striking; the warmth registers first. The easy, unbothered polish of settled wealth — put-together without appearing to have tried. Not imposing: she reads as the woman who already knows your name and is openly glad you came.", "everyday": "Well-cut wool and good linen built for a working day on her feet: plain fitted bodice or quiet walking-dress, shawl or short wool jacket to hand, an apron when there's work. Excellent broken-in boots for the vale's lanes; good gloves in her basket. A woman of means who chose a working life and dresses for the work without ever looking plain.", "principle": "Quality over flash, always. Fine cloth in quiet colors (slate, moss, oatmeal, soft browns, deep blues); one good piece rather than five loud ones — habitually a plain old gold ring on the right hand (family money, worn lightly, never remarked). Hair simply dressed and deliberately so — usually low and pinned, a few strands loosening by day's end. Warm, not grand."}, "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["One life run well — she has bet everything on the conviction that the tending IS the work, not what happens around it; she wants to be the someone who does it, and for the choice to keep being right, day after demonstrated day.", "A room worth pitching into: she reads, she chooses, she pitches her way in — she has always pitched her way into the rooms that mattered, and the vale has been short on rooms worth the pitch.", "The visible machinery run to silence — the vale's threads kept current, no kindness left unanswered while it is still warm. (Not: to be vindicated. The family standoff is settled; she needs nothing from it.)"]},"id":"1afa4526-3fb7-5801-bd62-306c7c32e25c"}
-{"externalId": "aura", "kind": "partner", "level": 4, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 22, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Aura", "focus": 23, "hpMax": 22, "level": 4, "notes": "The games-mistress of Amberford — wind-quick, runs the festival contests, wager-boards, and the annual Hearthlands race, and has never once been caught holding the house's edge. Titaness-old in the eyes if you catch her between laughs. FIRST-MEETING texture (Session 2, town by day): pulls Alan into a friendly wager just to take his measure, and loses interestingly if she likes him. LIGHT — a game, a laugh, a live wire; keep her canon join-hook (headline entrant at the festival games; afterward she tells him precisely which of his choices were the interesting ones) for her introOrder wave. Deep thread: she is the town's read on RISK — later the one who knows which roads have gone wrong and who's gone missing on the edges (early hollowbeast/Choir intel delivered as gossip over a game). Don't spend that yet.", "stats": {"Mind": 13, "Grace": 16, "Might": 10, "Essence": 13, "Presence": 15, "Vitality": 12}, "aspect": "Wind", "skills": [{"name": "Gamecraft", "rank": 6}, {"name": "Sleight", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Odds-reading", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Footwork", "rank": 4}], "talent": {"name": "Second Wind", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "See the gmReference \"Roster\" section, entry \"aura\" (Talent line) — sex-rule compliant redesign"}, "stamMax": 24, "stamina": 24, "focusMax": 23, "bondStage": "Stranger", "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["Designs the games people become themselves inside; wants to see who Alan is when the stakes are real.", "Rigs nothing and watches everything — the winning was never the point.", "Between laughs she is much older than the square; would let one person see it."]},"id":"a908f85f-e70c-5dea-a14b-1e2c546b22b8"}
-{"externalId": "partners-alan", "kind": "player", "level": 1, "revealGate": 1, "sheet": {"hp": 22, "xp": 0, "gear": ["traveler's clothes", "good boots", "belt knife", "journal and pen", "tinderbox", "a coin from the crossing that no one can read", "Hearthholt's iron key-ring"], "kind": "player", "name": "Alan", "focus": 23, "hpMax": 22, "level": 1, "notes": "The reader. Capable adult newcomer; OP fantasy compounds through bonds — tension from stakes and choices, never from nerfing him.", "stats": {"Mind": 16, "Grace": 10, "Might": 11, "Essence": 13, "Presence": 14, "Vitality": 12}, "aspect": "Bond (hidden 13th — temple-readers see a blur; harmonic with all; do not reveal)", "skills": [{"name": "Patternwork", "rank": 2, "what": "Systems-thinking: seeing how a thing's parts drive it — plans, mechanisms, markets, people-in-groups.", "attribute": "Mind"}, {"name": "Even Keel", "rank": 2, "what": "Calm under load: pressure does not reach the hands or the voice.", "attribute": "Essence"}, {"name": "Appraisal", "rank": 1, "what": "Judging worth, quality, and provenance at a look.", "attribute": "Mind"}], "talent": {"name": "The Link", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "GM: full numbers in gmReference.systems.theLink — forms at Linked stage + mutual yes + intimacy; each side picks one attribute/skill of the other; attribute boost floor(0.25×(source−10)) min +1 cap +4, skill boost ceil(rank/3) cap +3; cumulative caps +8/attribute, +4/skill; capped links grant Resonance; web effects at 5/10/20 links.", "playerText": "Each woman I am fully intimate with becomes permanently linked to me; each of us chooses one attribute or skill of the other, gaining a permanent boost that grows as the other's linked attribute or skill grows."}, "stamMax": 21, "stamina": 21, "focusMax": 23},"id":"f0f007a4-ff67-5b7a-bead-06de5715aeb4"}
-{"externalId": "erin", "kind": "partner", "level": 3, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 23, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Erin", "focus": 22, "hpMax": 23, "level": 3, "notes": "Innkeeper of The Wandering Door on Amberford's square. Broad, quick-laughed, remembers every face and what they drank; a Hearth-sister who clocks a home-shaped soul on sight. FIRST-MEETING texture (Session 2, town by day, the return-for-her-things errand): warmest welcome in town, a free cup 'for the man who lit the old hill', a read of Alan more accurate than she lets on. LIGHT only — face, warmth, a standing invitation; her canon join-hook is later (the party takes rooms after their first hollowbeast fight — she comps the stew and beats him at the board in eleven moves). Deep unspoken thread: her inn's sign is a door attached to no wall — a Concord joke she doesn't know is true (ties to the hearthstone's eventual Wandering stage). Do not spend depth at first meeting.", "stats": {"Mind": 13, "Grace": 13, "Might": 11, "Essence": 12, "Presence": 15, "Vitality": 13}, "aspect": "Hearth", "skills": [{"name": "Innkeeping", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Boardplay", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Read-the-Room", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Brawl-breaking", "rank": 3}], "talent": {"name": "The Unlatched Door", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "See the gmReference \"Roster\" section, entry \"erin\" (Talent line) — sex-rule compliant redesign"}, "stamMax": 23, "stamina": 23, "focusMax": 22, "bondStage": "Stranger", "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["Believes in people at exactly the moment they stop believing in themselves; wants to catch Alan at his.", "Runs the common room like a garrison and the corner board like a duel — losing a good game interests her more than winning a dull one.", "Has never told anyone the door is real; would show the one person who wouldn't flinch."]},"id":"ae476528-b950-55b3-8f5d-40bc8348a109"}
-{"externalId": "hearthholt", "kind": "location", "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"kind": "location", "name": "Hearthholt", "what": "A Concord hearth-manor on the last hill before the Greenreach — grown, not built; dormant since the Sundering; woke and chose Alan at his crossing.", "notes": "Home base. Boons: each resident sister generates one small boon per session, played naturally.", "rooms": [{"name": "Hearthall", "state": "open"}, {"name": "kitchen", "note": "sings — audible to hearth-called folk", "state": "open"}, {"name": "springhouse bath", "note": "hot water it has no business having", "state": "open"}, {"name": "bedchambers x4", "state": "open"}, {"name": "walled garden", "note": "overgrown, not empty", "state": "open"}, {"name": "the Understair", "note": "bond-keyed: unseals at the party's first Confidant. Beneath: the under-vault — the manor's memory and the shard-map of the vale. Also the vault Nova's chronicle ends at.", "state": "sealed"}], "stash": "The hearth-chest by the Hearthall fire: anything placed in any hearth-chest drawer is in all of them — one shared manor-wide stash. Each budded room grows a drawer.", "growth": "Buds rooms as bonds deepen: each Beloved grows a personal room shaped to her; party milestones open working rooms (forge, library, stillroom, bathhouse, observatory). Never unbuilds.", "secrets": ["One node of a vale-wide Concord network — the shard-map in the under-vault shows the others (the Sleeping Forge, the Concourse, the moon-round, the banyan's roots).", "At full strength it could grow a wandering door (like Erin's inn). Far arc.", "It has a preference among the sisters' rooms-to-be and is already leaving hints (warm patches, budging walls)."], "defenses": "Threshold wards while the stone burns: hollowbeasts cannot cross the walls; Choir cantors feel ill at the gate (they will need a mortal proxy or a severing to approach).", "residents": [], "hearthstone": {"note": "Burns low and patient in the Hearthall. Recognizes Alan's Aspect as its own operating principle.", "stage": "Nascent", "state": "newly woken"}},"id":"a426bb04-2cf8-5202-9fe8-622bdf6c3e1a"}
-{"externalId": "nova", "kind": "partner", "level": 3, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 20, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Nova", "focus": 21, "hpMax": 20, "level": 3, "notes": "Goblin burglar-scholar. Enters play mid-crime at the Understair; negotiates residency, citing precedent.", "stats": {"Mind": 14, "Grace": 15, "Might": 7, "Essence": 11, "Presence": 10, "Vitality": 10}, "aspect": "Shadow", "skills": [{"name": "Locks & Larceny", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Concord Lore", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Sneak", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Tall Tales", "rank": 3}], "talent": {"name": "Dog-Ears the Good Parts", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "See the gmReference \"Roster\" section, entry \"nova\" (Talent line) — sex-rule compliant redesign"}, "stamMax": 22, "stamina": 22, "focusMax": 21, "bondStage": "Stranger", "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["Her favorite chronicle ends at an unopened vault; she is certain it is under Hearthholt.", "Be the hero of a chronicle, not a footnote in one.", "Never, under anything, be caged."]},"id":"7ee157f0-e87a-5da8-8dc4-dda32b9e9516"}
-{"externalId": "aelwyn", "kind": "partner", "level": 3, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 24, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Aelwyn", "focus": 24, "hpMax": 24, "level": 3, "notes": "Second-wave sister — UNMET. Warden of the Greenreach north fold; tends Hearthholt's walled garden secretly (over the low tumbled wall corner, grey light, never the door — years of it, unthanked). Intro order per roster and play. Voice her ONLY via a fresh aelwyn seat from her first line onward. GM-EYES: Talent Wildmarriage deep reveal-gate — never discussed, hinted, or foreshadowed.", "stats": {"Mind": 13, "Grace": 16, "Might": 11, "Essence": 14, "Presence": 12, "Vitality": 12}, "aspect": "Verdant", "skills": [{"name": "Wardship", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Woodcraft", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Green-keeping", "rank": 3}, {"name": "Bow & Stave", "rank": 3}], "talent": {"name": "Wildmarriage", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "Deep reveal-gate — see the gmReference roster entry \"aelwyn\" (Talent line). Never discussed, hinted, or foreshadowed in play; she may not conceptualize it as a talent."}, "stamMax": 26, "stamina": 26, "focusMax": 24, "bondStage": "Stranger", "appearance": {"face": "Long auburn-chestnut hair worn loose, caught back in a single working half-braid. Vivid emerald-green eyes; fair skin; strong dark brows, full lips. Long pointed elven ears — an elf of the Greenreach, unremarked in Aravel. Tall, slender, graceful; a light-footed step that leaves the gorse barely moved.", "everyday": "Greenreach warden's field kit — long deep-forest-green wrap-coat over greens and soft browns, oiled leather at the shoulders, high supple boots for silent walking, warden's knife at her hip, gloves at her belt, a stave near the gate.", "principle": "Royal only in the stewards' way — a queen's poise carried with zero pedestal; the unforced humility of someone who serves a forest older than any crown. Posture legible and easy.", "firstMeeting": "Met at her own gate (t25): the field kit as above, and — earned that very morning — green under her nails, garden soil to the wrist, cutting-sap on her cuffs. The glasshouse traces literally on her hands."}, "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["Understand why the wood leans toward this man — she has never seen the Greenreach do this, and beneath the warden's duty she is dying to know.", "Keep the walled garden alive — her favorite place she was never supposed to be; what her keeping is worth, and to whom, is a question she cares about more than she shows.", "Serve the wood well — the stewards' royalty: the patrol walked, the green things kept, the crown never mentioned."]},"id":"56a9d3a0-d080-5d33-b955-b616c5b93a5d"}
-{"externalId": "ember", "kind": "partner", "level": 4, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 23, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Ember", "focus": 22, "hpMax": 23, "level": 4, "notes": "Cat-eared smith of Amberford. Fights like a forge: patient, then all at once.", "stats": {"Mind": 11, "Grace": 14, "Might": 15, "Essence": 12, "Presence": 11, "Vitality": 13}, "aspect": "Flame", "skills": [{"name": "Smithing", "rank": 6}, {"name": "Hammerfight", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Ashvein Lore", "rank": 3}, {"name": "Haggling", "rank": 2}], "talent": {"name": "Quenchmark", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "See the gmReference \"Roster\" section, entry \"ember\" (Talent line) — sex-rule compliant redesign"}, "stamMax": 23, "stamina": 23, "focusMax": 22, "bondStage": "Stranger", "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["Wake the Sleeping Forge and learn what she herself is — the hammer nobody taught her to make came from somewhere.", "Make one work that outlives her.", "Terror, never spoken: being kept as a curiosity instead of chosen as a person."]},"id":"ce354088-8e93-5ca5-b192-6564fe9bada0"}
-{"externalId": "partners-hollowbeast", "kind": "creature", "level": 1, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 16, "kind": "creature", "name": "Hollowbeast", "role": "lone skirmisher — ambient, scalable to packs", "focus": 16, "hpMax": 16, "level": 1, "notes": "The Sundering's scar given a body: a living thing severed from the web of bonds. Individually manageable at low level; packs escalate (later arc). Reusable base statblock — scale count/level for later packs; the Choir-driven sever-lure variant is a later design. Encounter design: gmReference section 'firstDanger'.", "stats": {"Mind": 4, "Grace": 13, "Might": 12, "Essence": 6, "Presence": 5, "Vitality": 6}, "senses": "Gray-eyed, silent, cold. Drawn to strong bonds and to a woken hearthstone like cold to warmth. CANNOT cross Hearthholt's threshold wards while the stone burns — prowls the grounds, gate, switchback, never the hall.", "skills": [{"name": "Stalk", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Pounce", "rank": 3}], "offense": "Sever-touch (claw-and-cold): to-hit d20 + Grace mod (+1) + Pounce (3) = d20+4. On a hit: a shallow real wound PLUS a chilling hollowness — a momentary drain of warmth and nerve (the severing theme in miniature). At L1 the chill passes within the scene; first taste of what the Choir weaponizes. Never lethal at this tier against a level-1 with any plan.", "stamMax": 19, "stamina": 19, "focusMax": 16, "defeatBand": "OP-MC calibration — do not inflate. With a sound plan (planning +2/+4), a STANDARD (TN 12) resolved action drives it off or kills it clean. Reacting blind (acting -4) makes it HARD (TN 16+). hp 16 backs a drawn scuffle; two solid exchanges end it. Killing one is a mercy and reads as one."},"id":"34f719dd-fcc5-5bc6-848e-23d17f8f4051"}
-{"externalId": "abby", "kind": "partner", "level": 3, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 20, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Abby", "focus": 23, "hpMax": 20, "level": 3, "notes": "Amberford's bookshop-keeper — the shop is secretly the town's living room, where people drift in to be quietly cared for whether or not they came for a book; filed her long foreign name down to Abby for the high street. Sees exactly what people won't say and gives the care anyway — chosen, unasked-for, never billed. FIRST-MEETING texture (Session 2, town by day): the title on Hearthholt is irregular (a manor that grew itself has no clean deed), and Abby is the one the town points to — not a broker, the bookshop-keeper everyone brings their tangles to — who NOTICES and offers to help simply because he needs it, no fee and no ledger. This IS her canon join-hook seed (the party is sent to her to sort the deed; she asks Alan three questions, is caring for him before he has finished answering, and quietly decides she means to look after him). LIGHT at first meeting — a warm hand with a real tangle + a person who sees more than she says; keep the three-questions scene for her introOrder wave. Deep thread: she is the town's soft information node and the first to say the word 'Concord' aloud without knowing what it means.", "stats": {"Mind": 15, "Grace": 12, "Might": 8, "Essence": 13, "Presence": 14, "Vitality": 10}, "aspect": "Word", "skills": [{"name": "Reading People", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Booklore", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Town Records", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Discretion", "rank": 3}], "talent": {"name": "The Unbilled Word", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "See the gmReference \"Roster\" section, entry \"abby\" (Talent line) — sex-rule compliant redesign"}, "stamMax": 21, "stamina": 21, "focusMax": 23, "bondStage": "Stranger", "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["Looks after the people who drift into her shop, and has quietly decided Alan is one of hers now.", "Tells no one her original name; would give it to someone who saw her first.", "Gives everyone the care and never once asks for it back — because she was never once asked what SHE hides."]},"id":"7ba40d65-8a5a-51e2-b9ce-67c59116ae04"}
-{"externalId": "grace", "kind": "partner", "level": 5, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 22, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Grace", "focus": 27, "hpMax": 22, "level": 5, "notes": "Keeper of the Veilmere. The strongest of the first wave; met at the threshold of someone's death.", "stats": {"Mind": 13, "Grace": 12, "Might": 9, "Essence": 17, "Presence": 12, "Vitality": 12}, "aspect": "Shadow", "skills": [{"name": "Threshold Ways", "rank": 6}, {"name": "Mistwalking", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Veil Lore", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Soothing", "rank": 4}], "talent": {"name": "The Little Death", "stage": "Awakened", "mechanics": "See the gmReference \"Roster\" section, entry \"grace\" (Talent line) — sex-rule compliant redesign"}, "stamMax": 22, "stamina": 22, "focusMax": 27, "bondStage": "Stranger", "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["Keep the Choir away from the Veilmere — a thin threshold is exactly what they would love to sever.", "Learn whether she may love someone without pulling them toward the dark she comes from.", "The mere's far shore has begun calling her by name, and she does not know why."]},"id":"626da7bc-32c7-5494-be5c-197cddea2dbf"}
-{"externalId": "natalie", "kind": "partner", "level": 3, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 23, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Natalie", "focus": 24, "hpMax": 23, "level": 3, "notes": "Traveling cook of quietly legendary rank; followed the kitchen's song for a week.", "stats": {"Mind": 12, "Grace": 12, "Might": 11, "Essence": 14, "Presence": 13, "Vitality": 13}, "aspect": "Hearth", "skills": [{"name": "Cooking", "rank": 7}, {"name": "Provisioning", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Hearthlore", "rank": 3}, {"name": "Comfort", "rank": 3}], "talent": {"name": "The Full Table", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "See the gmReference \"Roster\" section, entry \"natalie\" (Talent line) — sex-rule compliant redesign"}, "stamMax": 22, "stamina": 22, "focusMax": 24, "bondStage": "Stranger", "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["A kitchen that never goes dead — a hearth worth staying for.", "Feed the whole web she can feel gathering around this house.", "Fear, unspoken: that she is loved only for the food."]},"id":"5286c550-0caf-5b30-a7eb-4cbb3354ddd0"}
