-{"external-id":"partners-ii-t001","turn-number":1,"status":"published","text":"Dusk, and a road you have never stood on before.\n\nThere is no seam to the crossing — no flash, no falling. One stride ago there was somewhere else, and now there is this: a packed-earth road running the spine of a green valley, hills folding away on either side under a sky going violet at the edges. The air is cool and smells of rain that fell an hour ago on someone else. Two moons are rising, one low and gold, one high and thin as a paring of silver.\n\nYou stop. You take stock, because that is what you do.\n\nYour clothes are your own. Your boots are your own, and dry. In your left pocket: a coin you have never seen, heavy, warm as a held hand, stamped with writing that refuses to resolve no matter how steadily you look at it. In your right: an iron key-ring you did not put there, old and honest, five keys of five different sizes, and a worn brass tag with a word you CAN read:\n\nHEARTHHOLT.\n\nAnd then the world notices you.\n\nIt arrives like a window catching lamplight — a pane of violet glass that is not glass, hanging in the air a polite arm's length away.\n\nIt names you. Your name, then a number that feels both insulting and fair. Then your skills, one by one, each landing like a stamp in a ledger: the pattern-sense, the steady hands, the appraiser's eye. The pane records you the way a clerk records a delivery — briskly, completely, without opinion.\n\nThen it reaches your talent, and prints one line more, in exactly the voice it printed everything else: no classification. No precedent on record.\n\nIt is you who pauses.\n\nYou read the line twice. It reads the same both times, and that is somehow the loudest thing on the pane: a ledger has just hit a blank where an entry should be, and the clerk has stamped the blank and moved on, and nothing in all that violet glass finds it worth a second look. You do. You are still looking when the pane folds itself away like a bird tucking a wing.\n\nAcross the valley, on a shoulder of hill above a river you can hear but not yet see, stands a house. Manor is the better word — stone below, dark timber above, a slate roof with too many chimneys for one household, windows dark save one. One window, high in the eastern gable, is lit. It was not lit a moment ago. You are certain of that the way you are certain of load-bearing walls.\n\nThe key-ring sits in your pocket with the specific weight of an answered question.\n\nThe road forks a stone's throw ahead. The left fork runs down the valley floor toward a far-off scatter of town lights, an hour's walk, maybe more, smoke standing up straight from chimneys into the still evening. The right fork climbs — switchbacked, hedged with something blooming white that you cannot name — to the manor's iron gate.\n\nYou are alone on the road. The evening is mild. Nothing hunts you. Nothing hurries you. The world, whatever it has decided about you, appears content to let you decide something back.\n\nBehind you the road runs flat and empty into the dusk, and it occurs to you — a fact, filed calmly, the way you file such things — that it does not go back to where you came from. Roads here go where they go. That one goes east.\n\nThe gold moon clears the hills. Somewhere below, the river turns over in its bed. The lit window across the valley waits — patient in a way the glass pane never was.","length":624,"published-at":"2026-07-10T01:45:51.482Z","word-count":624,"session-number":1,"sheet-snapshot":{"hud":{"level":1,"pools":{"hp":22,"focus":23,"hpMax":22,"stamMax":21,"stamina":21,"focusMax":23}},"log":[{"id":1,"text":"You cross into Aravel mid-stride: a valley road at dusk, two moons rising, a warm unreadable coin and an iron key-ring you did not put in your pockets.","turn":1,"type":"narrative"},{"id":2,"turn":1,"type":"system","lines":["Registered: ALAN — Level 1.","Talent: THE LINK — classification: none. No precedent on record."],"title":"Aravel greets the traveler"},{"id":3,"text":"Across the valley a manor stands on a shoulder of hill — Hearthholt, says the brass tag. One high window is lit. It was not lit a moment ago. The road forks: down toward distant town lights, or up to the iron gate.","turn":1,"type":"narrative"}],"turn":1,"chapters":[{"title":"The Crossing","number":1,"status":"open","endBeat":3,"chapterId":"partners-t001","startBeat":1}],"revealed":{"kind":"player","name":"Alan","class":"Wanderer","level":1,"skills":[{"name":"Patternwork","note":"Systems-thinking: seeing how a thing's parts drive it — plans, mechanisms, markets, people-in-groups.","rung":"Rank 2"},{"name":"Even Keel","note":"Calm under load: pressure does not reach the hands or the voice.","rung":"Rank 2"},{"name":"Appraisal","note":"Judging worth, quality, and provenance at a look.","rung":"Rank 1"}],"titles":[{"name":"Talent: The Link","note":"Each woman I am fully intimate with becomes permanently linked to me; each of us chooses one attribute or skill of the other, gaining a permanent boost that grows as the other's linked attribute or skill grows. — Classification: none. No precedent on record."}],"derived":{"Stamina":21,"Vitality (HP)":22,"Essence (Focus)":23},"inventory":[{"name":"Traveler's clothes and good boots"},{"name":"Belt knife"},{"name":"Journal and pen"},{"name":"Tinderbox"},{"name":"A coin from the crossing","note":"Warm. Unreadable."},{"name":"Hearthholt's iron key-ring","note":"Five keys. One brass tag."}],"affinities":[{"name":"Aspect","note":"Unread. Temple-readers see only a blur, and find this upsetting.","value":"—"}],"attributes":{"MIND":16,"GRACE":10,"MIGHT":11,"ESSENCE":13,"PRESENCE":14,"VITALITY":12}}},"gate-verdict":{"detail":{"povNotes":"Single fixed close POV (Alan), second person. Consistent with partners-ii's viewpoint default; no dual/rotating interiority, no omniscient framing.","watchItems":"window-pane-prose: the arrival set-piece carries a high density of buttoned paragraph-closers; individually reveal-bearing and earned at a genuine peak, but worth watching cross-turn for a habitual button-cadence once K>=3.","suspensions":{"intimacy-register":"no intimate content in turn 1"},"notSuspended":"system-voice, channel-separation, impartial-arbiter all judged in-scope (partners-ii has mechanics and a mute/undeclared System).","crossTurnTallies":{"K":0,"note":"Turn 1 of the run; no prior published turns. cadence-tell, turn-boundaries, and show-dont-tell are clean-by-insufficient-history — a single turn cannot form a K>=3 uniform run, and none violates independently.","showDontTellPriorTheses":"none (no prior turns)","turnBoundaryClassification":{"head":"in-motion / perception (arrival)","close":"poised (decision handed to player at the fork)"}},"retconAttestation":"Re-gate of the doctrine-v7 awed-System repair. The current published text renders the Crossing System-pane FLAT; every committed fact (two moons, warm unreadable coin, HEARTHHOLT five-key ring, unlit-then-lit eastern-gable window, one-way road east, unclassifiable talent) is preserved. Drama lives entirely in the PC reading an indifferent instrument. system-voice CONFIRMED clean."},"overall":"PASS","attempts":1,"findings":[{"verdict":"clean","evidence":"Second-person POV bound throughout to Alan's perception/fallible inference: 'a number that feels both insulting and fair', 'You are certain of that the way you are certain of load-bearing walls'. No other mind's interiority is leaked (no NPCs present); the System is an instrument, not a mind. Ambient reads ('Nothing hunts you') are POV inference, not asserted outside-vantage truth.","dimension":"perceivable-bound"},{"verdict":"clean","evidence":"Turn 1: no prior turns to recap. Head opens mid-fiction on arrival ('Dusk, and a road you have never stood on before'), not recap-scaffolding; close lands on an in-fiction image ('The lit window across the valley waits — patient in a way the glass pane never was'), not wind-down-to-end scaffolding.","dimension":"invisible-turns:boundary-seam"},{"verdict":"clean","evidence":"No narrator-voice solicitation of next input. The fork is described as world geography ('The road forks a stone's throw ahead...'), which legally closes a beat; the actual final line is an image (moon/river/window), not a 'what do you do?' handoff. Decision-point framing without a prompt line.","dimension":"invisible-turns:invitation-close"},{"verdict":"clean","evidence":"The System encounter narrates the EFFECT, never stat tokens or sheet-register. Skills surface as perception ('the pattern-sense, the steady hands, the appraiser's eye'), the level as an oblique reaction ('a number that feels both insulting and fair') — no verbatim numbers, no 'behind glass'/'bookkeeping' bleed. Consistent with partners' channel rule (narrate the experience of a readout, never restate its text).","dimension":"invisible-turns:mechanical-echo"},{"verdict":"clean","evidence":"No reference to turns, rolls, action bar, or retries as apparatus anywhere in the prose. The violet pane is a diegetic in-fiction object, not a UI/meta frame.","dimension":"invisible-turns:meta-leak"},{"verdict":"clean","evidence":"Cross-turn dimension. Tally: no prior published turns in the run (K=0, this is turn 1). A single-turn run cannot exhibit a K>=3 uniform-shape pulse; clean-by-insufficient-history — the one turn does not independently violate.","dimension":"invisible-turns:cadence-tell"},{"verdict":"clean","evidence":"No laundered agency: the consequential decision (which fork) is explicitly left to the player ('The world... appears content to let you decide something back'). 'You stop. You take stock, because that is what you do' is scene-establishment of the established appraiser PC, not an unchosen consequential action. No mechanics invoked, so no success-by-phrasing. Turn 1 scene-set is genre-appropriate.","dimension":"emergent-story-dm-register"},{"verdict":"clean","evidence":"Emotional pitch tracks the moment — no constant superlatives. The peak be