+{"externalId": "amy", "kind": "partner", "level": 1, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 20, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Amy", "role": "The vale's quiet connector — Amberford. Looks after rather a lot of things, none of them hers; Hearthholt's affairs (taxes, gutters, chimneys swept for no one) one thread among hundreds, kept well because she keeps everything well.", "focus": 22, "hpMax": 20, "level": 1, "notes": "First sister — UNMET, intro order 1. Intro hook: the keys leave her locked drawer at dusk the moment he crosses; she climbs the hill the same evening with supper packed before she knows whom she'll meet (Kept's first-ever firing — her hands sure of a stranger; she will not know what it means). Voice her ONLY via the fresh amy seat from her first line onward (gmContext policy amy-seat-voice). GM-EYES: Kept fate-basis is deep fog.", "stats": {"Mind": 15, "Grace": 11, "Might": 8, "Essence": 12, "Presence": 14, "Vitality": 10}, "aspect": "Hearth", "skills": [{"name": "Stewardship", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Reading People", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Provisioning", "rank": 3}, {"name": "Letters & Accounts", "rank": 2}], "talent": {"name": "Kept", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "Fate-based: fires for anyone she is GOING to have sex with in the future, before either knows — see the gmReference roster entry \"amy\" (Talent line). It has NEVER YET FIRED; she does not know she carries it in these terms."}, "stamMax": 20, "stamina": 20, "focusMax": 22, "bondStage": "Stranger", "appearance": {"face": "Blonde, fair-skinned — coloring that takes lamplight and morning light kindly. Blue eyes that do most of her listening: steady, warm, attentive; you feel read before you feel looked at. Handsome rather than striking; the warmth registers first. The easy, unbothered polish of settled wealth — put-together without appearing to have tried. Not imposing: she reads as the woman who already knows your name and is openly glad you came.", "everyday": "Well-cut wool and good linen built for a working day on her feet: plain fitted bodice or quiet walking-dress, shawl or short wool jacket to hand, an apron when there's work. Excellent broken-in boots for the vale's lanes; good gloves in her basket. A woman of means who chose a working life and dresses for the work without ever looking plain.", "principle": "Quality over flash, always. Fine cloth in quiet colors (slate, moss, oatmeal, soft browns, deep blues); one good piece rather than five loud ones — habitually a plain old gold ring on the right hand (family money, worn lightly, never remarked). Hair simply dressed and deliberately so — usually low and pinned, a few strands loosening by day's end. Warm, not grand."}, "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["One life run well — she has bet everything on the conviction that the tending IS the work, not what happens around it; she wants to be the someone who does it, and for the choice to keep being right, day after demonstrated day.", "A room worth pitching into: she reads, she chooses, she pitches her way in — she has always pitched her way into the rooms that mattered, and the vale has been short on rooms worth the pitch.", "The visible machinery run to silence — the vale's threads kept current, no kindness left unanswered while it is still warm. (Not: to be vindicated. The family standoff is settled; she needs nothing from it.)"]},"id":"1afa4526-3fb7-5801-bd62-306c7c32e25c"}
+{"externalId": "aura", "kind": "partner", "level": 4, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 22, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Aura", "focus": 23, "hpMax": 22, "level": 4, "notes": "The games-mistress of Amberford — wind-quick, runs the festival contests, wager-boards, and the annual Hearthlands race, and has never once been caught holding the house's edge. Titaness-old in the eyes if you catch her between laughs. FIRST-MEETING texture (Session 2, town by day): pulls Alan into a friendly wager just to take his measure, and loses interestingly if she likes him. LIGHT — a game, a laugh, a live wire; keep her canon join-hook (headline entrant at the festival games; afterward she tells him precisely which of his choices were the interesting ones) for her introOrder wave. Deep thread: she is the town's read on RISK — later the one who knows which roads have gone wrong and who's gone missing on the edges (early hollowbeast/Choir intel delivered as gossip over a game). Don't spend that yet.", "stats": {"Mind": 13, "Grace": 16, "Might": 10, "Essence": 13, "Presence": 15, "Vitality": 12}, "aspect": "Wind", "skills": [{"name": "Gamecraft", "rank": 6}, {"name": "Sleight", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Odds-reading", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Footwork", "rank": 4}], "talent": {"name": "Second Wind", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "See the gmReference \"Roster\" section, entry \"aura\" (Talent line) — sex-rule compliant redesign"}, "stamMax": 24, "stamina": 24, "focusMax": 23, "bondStage": "Stranger", "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["Designs the games people become themselves inside; wants to see who Alan is when the stakes are real.", "Rigs nothing and watches everything — the winning was never the point.", "Between laughs she is much older than the square; would let one person see it."]},"id":"a908f85f-e70c-5dea-a14b-1e2c546b22b8"}
