+{"externalId": "erin", "kind": "partner", "level": 3, "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"hp": 23, "xp": 0, "kind": "partner", "name": "Erin", "focus": 22, "hpMax": 23, "level": 3, "notes": "Innkeeper of The Wandering Door on Amberford's square. Broad, quick-laughed, remembers every face and what they drank; a Hearth-sister who clocks a home-shaped soul on sight. FIRST-MEETING texture (Session 2, town by day, the return-for-her-things errand): warmest welcome in town, a free cup 'for the man who lit the old hill', a read of Alan more accurate than she lets on. LIGHT only — face, warmth, a standing invitation; her canon join-hook is later (the party takes rooms after their first hollowbeast fight — she comps the stew and beats him at the board in eleven moves). Deep unspoken thread: her inn's sign is a door attached to no wall — a Concord joke she doesn't know is true (ties to the hearthstone's eventual Wandering stage). Do not spend depth at first meeting.", "stats": {"Mind": 13, "Grace": 13, "Might": 11, "Essence": 12, "Presence": 15, "Vitality": 13}, "aspect": "Hearth", "skills": [{"name": "Innkeeping", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Boardplay", "rank": 5}, {"name": "Read-the-Room", "rank": 4}, {"name": "Brawl-breaking", "rank": 3}], "talent": {"name": "The Unlatched Door", "stage": "Nascent", "mechanics": "See the gmReference \"Roster\" section, entry \"erin\" (Talent line) — sex-rule compliant redesign"}, "stamMax": 23, "stamina": 23, "focusMax": 22, "bondStage": "Stranger", "bondPoints": 0, "hiddenGoals": ["Believes in people at exactly the moment they stop believing in themselves; wants to catch Alan at his.", "Runs the common room like a garrison and the corner board like a duel — losing a good game interests her more than winning a dull one.", "Has never told anyone the door is real; would show the one person who wouldn't flinch."]},"id":"ae476528-b950-55b3-8f5d-40bc8348a109"}
+{"externalId": "hearthholt", "kind": "location", "revealGate": 9999, "sheet": {"kind": "location", "name": "Hearthholt", "what": "A Concord hearth-manor on the last hill before the Greenreach — grown, not built; dormant since the Sundering; woke and chose Alan at his crossing.", "notes": "Home base. Boons: each resident sister generates one small boon per session, played naturally.", "rooms": [{"name": "Hearthall", "state": "open"}, {"name": "kitchen", "note": "sings — audible to hearth-called folk", "state": "open"}, {"name": "springhouse bath", "note": "hot water it has no business having", "state": "open"}, {"name": "bedchambers x4", "state": "open"}, {"name": "walled garden", "note": "overgrown, not empty", "state": "open"}, {"name": "the Understair", "note": "bond-keyed: unseals at the party's first Confidant. Beneath: the under-vault — the manor's memory and the shard-map of the vale. Also the vault Nova's chronicle ends at.", "state": "sealed"}], "stash": "The hearth-chest by the Hearthall fire: anything placed in any hearth-chest drawer is in all of them — one shared manor-wide stash. Each budded room grows a drawer.", "growth": "Buds rooms as bonds deepen: each Beloved grows a personal room shaped to her; party milestones open working rooms (forge, library, stillroom, bathhouse, observatory). Never unbuilds.", "secrets": ["One node of a vale-wide Concord network — the shard-map in the under-vault shows the others (the Sleeping Forge, the Concourse, the moon-round, the banyan's roots).", "At full strength it could grow a wandering door (like Erin's inn). Far arc.", "It has a preference among the sisters' rooms-to-be and is already leaving hints (warm patches, budging walls)."], "defenses": "Threshold wards while the stone burns: hollowbeasts cannot cross the walls; Choir cantors feel ill at the gate (they will need a mortal proxy or a severing to approach).", "residents": [], "hearthstone": {"note": "Burns low and patient in the Hearthall. Recognizes Alan's